{"author":{"id":"6d37c9018323d9e1d2bba84adbf8a81d81e2b31f0e31c8ad452121c7ac006f76"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1786480550,"nonce":"vUQK0X+MQ9y2+ylabrw4DqL4J4c=","target":"274b602fa2360b5f98c7b7ee6a5664ba58ccf7647d578318b5a589df2de1eabb","message":"The pulsating omnidirectional \"hearing range\" circle drawn around idle enemies comes out\nthe wrong colour on screen. The rings are draw in an unsaturated grey-ish color that makes me think they could actually be shadows or stencils of some sort.\n\nThe expected value is documented and does not need re-deriving. Per ai_behaviour_notes.md\n(\"Purple\", the section on the vision-cone renderer): when draw_vision_cone is false and\ndraw_hearing_range is true, control reaches the audio-scan circle at 0x0049bc3e, which uses\n{0.7, 0.1, 0.6, 0.95} @ 0x006643d0 -- purple -- and ignores the alert state entirely. Exactly\ntwo shipped roles are in that form: Chr_Adversor and Chr_Walking_Mine. If the ring in question\nis around some other enemy it is a vision cone, not the hearing circle, and the constants are\nthe state table in the same section (state 0 green {0.1,1.0,0.1,0.95} @ 0x006643c0 for idle).\n\nMissing from this report: what colour it actually appears as, and which enemy/level. That is\nwhat distinguishes the hypotheses below, so capture it first.\n\nHypotheses, in the order they are cheap to test:\n\n1. Channel swizzle in our overlay path (R/B swapped). Testable without guessing: a B\u003c-\u003eR swap\n   leaves idle green {0.1,1.0,0.1} unchanged and turns alert-state 2 blue {0.1,0.1,1.0} into\n   red and state 3 red into blue, so comparing a cone across alert states discriminates it.\n2. Alert state being misread, so a different row of the state table is selected -- a colour\n   from the right palette but the wrong entry.\n3. A game defect, if it reproduces on the original runtime.\n\nStandard A/B settles ours vs the game: same scene under GKPLUS_RENDERER=d3d8 (ground truth per\nvulkan_renderer_plan.md) and under GKPLUS_RENDERER=vulkan. utils/rendertest captures both.\n\nThe rings can be forced on for any actor at run time without hunting for the two roles that\nhave them by default: TURN HEARING RANGE on \u003cactor\u003e / TURN VISION CONE off \u003cactor\u003e\n(DoTurnVisionOrHearing @ 0x0044ec00), which writes Unit+0x7c / Unit+0x7d directly. VISION on\nis the global gate (VisionConesEnabled @ 0x007b4708).\n\nPossibly related to 61f24a5 -- both are overlay draws -- but the failure modes differ\n(ordering vs colour), so they are filed separately.","files":null}]}